ee of $312K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $65K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $55K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 47\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Andersen Group Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.2B market cap on $839M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -64% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $174M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -94.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 18.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 18% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 34% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3391068252036329},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5438745.82},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Andersen (ANDG) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/andersen-andg-q3-2026-earnings-074614000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794556510.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Andersen Group Inc (ANDG) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Revenue Jumps 18. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/andersen-group-inc-andg-q3-050145075.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546105.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Andersen Group (ANDG) Lifted Guidance And Added Acquisitions, Is It Still Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-andg/andersen-group/news/andersen-group-andg-lifted-guidance-and-added-acquisitions-i","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794536675.559,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"comp